{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Am]Way down in Columbus Georgia
Lord I'm [E7]wishing I was back in [Am]Tennessee
[Am]Way down in that old Columbus Stockade
My [E7]friends all have turned their backs on [Am]me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Dm]Go and leave me if you [Am]wish to
[Dm]Never let me cross your [E7]mind
In your [Am]heart you love another
[E7]Leave me, little darling, I don't [Am]mind
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Many a night with you I've rambled
Honey, countless hours with you I've spent
Thought I had your sweet love and your little heart forever
And now I find it was only lent.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Last night as I lay sleeping
I am dreaming that I am lying in your arms
